-@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
-+## Changed
-+
-+- Added `src/lint/entry.rs`, implementing rust-lint "Lint entry paths": tasks
-+  are reread in the warnings' numeric order, their `entry` lists are checked
-+  against the change folder, the task and earlier scopes, the project tree or
-+  default branch, and other approved or archived changes, and each miss gives
-+  the requirement's error.
-+- Provider 4 reads a change's state in this crate: landed from the default
-+  branch's archive folder, then its `osq/<folder>` branch marker, then its
-+  stacked folder, then its checkout active/archive marker when git is on;
-+  with git off it reads only the checkout markers. Other changes come from
-+  rust-storage `list_changes`.
-+- Wired the entry findings into `lint.rs` between the per-task errors and the
-+  cross-task warnings, in both the parsed-proposal path and the invalid
-+  frontmatter path.
-+- Added `tests/lint_entry_paths.rs`, proving every row of "Entry path findings"
-+  plus the provider and brace guards on fresh `tests/copy/mod.rs` copies, and
-+  `tests/lint_entry_git.rs`, proving "Entry paths with git on" in scratch
-+  repositories made with `git init -b main` and a fixed author, plus branch,
-+  checkout, stacked, landed, unapproved and nested-project cases.
-+- Task verify `cargo test -p osq-feature-lint --test lint_entry_paths --test
-+  lint_entry_git --test lint_task_rules` passes.
-+- `cargo test -p osq-feature-lint` passes, so every existing lint test still
-+  passes unchanged.
-+- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` passes with `OSQ_CHANGE` set; its mutation step
-+  is skipped without `OSQ_DIFF`.
-+- Manual `cargo mutants -p osq-feature-lint` over `entry.rs` reports 60 caught,
-+  4 unviable and no missed mutant; over `lint.rs` it reports 23 caught, 7
-+  unviable and no missed mutant.
-+
-+## Deviated
-+
-+- A task whose `scope` or `entry` already holds a brace group stays out of the
-+  entry rule. The existing `lint_task_rules` scenario row for brace groups
-+  expects only the two brace errors, but its non-brace entry would also be
-+  missing; task 3 may not edit that test, so the task is skipped for entry
-+  findings. New rows prove both the brace skip and the otherwise unchanged
-+  checking of entries.
-+- In the git scenario's uncommitted-file row, `crates/delta/src/local.rs` holds
-+  a valid `Implements:` tag rather than the table's `x`. Rust `lint` runs the
-+  link gates after the entry rule, and an untagged Rust file adds a link-gate
-+  finding the scenario does not expect. The entry behaviour under test is
-+  unchanged.
-+
-+## Missing context
-+
-+- The delta spec's "Task rule findings" brace row and "Lint entry paths"
-+  conflict: the first expects no entry findings for `crates/**/entry` and
-+  `crates/{x,y}/lib.rs`, while the second would report them. The task scope
-+  excludes `tests/lint_task_rules.rs`, so the implementation resolves the
-+  conflict by skipping a task that already has a brace group finding.
-+
-+Touched: crates/features/lint/src/lint.rs, crates/features/lint/src/lint/entry.rs, crates/features/lint/tests/lint_entry_paths.rs, crates/features/lint/tests/lint_entry_git.rs
